SIMPLE("qr_text","Text to QR Code Generator – Free, Plain Text QR",
 "Convert any text to a QR code free: notes, codes, instructions or messages that show on scan, no internet needed. UTF-8, logo, colours, SVG. No sign-up.",
 "Text to QR code turns any plain text – a note, serial number, instructions, a poem, a product code or a short message – into a QR code. When scanned, the text is shown on screen. No website or internet connection is needed, which makes text codes great for offline equipment labels, treasure hunts, classroom activities and inventory tags.",
 ["Type or paste your text.","Keep the text short for an easy-to-scan code.","Style it and download PNG or SVG.","Scan to check the text appears correctly."],
 "The code contains the text itself. A QR code can hold up to 2,953 bytes in its largest version (fewer characters for non-Latin scripts, as each takes 2–4 bytes in UTF-8). In practice, keep it under about 300 characters: longer text creates a very dense code that needs to be printed large.",
 ["Equipment and asset labels with serial numbers","Escape rooms and treasure hunts","Classroom quizzes and answers","Museum and garden information points","Secret messages and greetings"],
 ["Use UTF-8 for accents and non-Latin scripts.","Long text? Link to a page instead with [URL to QR code](/url-to-qr-code/).","Print dense codes larger.","Avoid sensitive information on public codes."],
 "Scan to read","the full text appears on screen","text",
 [Q("How do I turn text into a QR code?","Type your text and download the code."),Q("How much text can a QR code hold?","Up to about 2,953 bytes, but under 300 characters scans best."),Q("Does it need internet to scan?","No, the text is inside the code."),Q("Can I use other languages?","Yes, UTF-8 supports all scripts."),Q("Is it free?","Yes."),Q("Can I add a logo?","Yes."),Q("Do codes expire?","No."),Q("Is my text uploaded?","No.")],
 [("URL to QR code","url-to-qr-code"),("Barcode generator","barcode-generator")])
SIMPLE("qr_url","URL to QR Code Generator – Free Link QR, No Expiry",
 "Turn any URL into a free QR code that never expires: website, menu, Google Form, YouTube, PDF link. Logo, colours, frame, SVG. No sign-up, no tracking.",
 "URL to QR code converts any web address into a QR code. Scanning opens the link in the phone's browser – a website, online menu, Google Form, YouTube video, review page, PDF, app-store page or payment link. The link is encoded directly, so there is no redirect, no tracking and no expiry date.",
 ["Paste the full URL including https://.","Shorten very long links for a simpler code (optional).","Style it, add a logo and a frame like *Scan me*.","Download PNG or SVG and test-scan before printing."],
 "The code contains your exact URL. Phones show a preview of the address before opening it, which also helps people trust the code. Because nothing is redirected, the link works as long as the page itself exists.",
 ["Restaurant menus and table tents","Posters, flyers and packaging","Google reviews and feedback forms","Event tickets and registration pages","Slides and printed reports linking to sources"],
 ["Always use https:// links.","Shorter URLs make cleaner codes.","Point to a page you control so you can update content without reprinting.","Add a call to action – people scan more when told why."],
 "Scan me","the correct page opens on the phone","URL",
 [Q("How do I create a QR code for a link?","Paste the URL and download the code."),Q("Do these QR codes expire?","No, the link is inside the code."),Q("Is it free?","Yes, with no limits or sign-up."),Q("Can I change the link later?","Not on a static code; point it at a page you can edit."),Q("Can I make a QR code for a Google Form or PDF?","Yes, paste its share link."),Q("Are scans tracked?","No."),Q("Can I add a logo?","Yes."),Q("PNG or SVG?","PNG for screens, SVG for print.")],
 [("Text to QR code","text-to-qr-code"),("Social media QR code","social-media-qr-code-generator")],
 [["Can people trust your QR code?","QR phishing (\"quishing\") has made some people cautious. Use your own domain, keep the URL readable in the scan preview, avoid unknown link shorteners and print your brand name next to the code. On public signs, check regularly that nobody has stuck a fake code over yours."]])
SIMPLE("qr_location","Location QR Code Generator – Google Maps & GPS",
 "Create a free location QR code: scan to open a GPS point in the phone's maps app. Latitude/longitude, logo, frame, SVG. No sign-up, never expires.",
 "A location QR code opens a place on the map when scanned, ready for directions. Use it on invitations, event signs, holiday-rental guides, delivery notes and shop flyers so people find you without searching for an address – especially useful for venues, trailheads and entrances that addresses do not describe well.",
 ["Enter latitude and longitude (from Google Maps: right-click the spot and copy the numbers).","Add a label if offered.","Style the code and add a frame like *Find us*.","Download and test-scan on iPhone and Android."],
 "The code contains a standard *geo:* URI, such as *geo:12.9716,77.5946*. Android opens it in Google Maps or another maps app; iPhones open Apple Maps or ask which app to use. Coordinates point to the exact spot – a car-park entrance or a side gate – rather than the centre of a street address.",
 ["Wedding and event invitations","Holiday rentals and campsites","Trailheads and meeting points","Delivery and pickup instructions","Shop and office flyers"],
 ["Use decimal coordinates (e.g. 51.5007, -0.1246).","Check the pin is on the right entrance.","Print the address as text too.","For a Google Maps place link, use [URL to QR code](/url-to-qr-code/)."],
 "Find us","the maps app opens at the right spot","location",
 [Q("How do I make a QR code for a location?","Enter the latitude and longitude and download the code."),Q("How do I find coordinates?","Right-click the spot in Google Maps; the numbers appear at the top of the menu."),Q("Does it open Google Maps?","On Android usually; iPhone opens Apple Maps or lets you choose."),Q("Is it free?","Yes."),Q("Can I link a Google Maps place instead?","Yes, paste its link into the URL QR tool."),Q("Do codes expire?","No."),Q("Is my location uploaded?","No."),Q("Can I add a logo?","Yes.")],
 [("Event QR code","event-qr-code-generator"),("URL to QR code","url-to-qr-code")])
SIMPLE("qr_email","Email QR Code Generator – Pre-filled Subject & Body",
 "Create a free email QR code: scan to open a new e-mail with address, subject and message pre-filled. Logo, colours, frame, SVG. No sign-up, never expires.",
 "An email QR code opens a new message in the phone's mail app with the recipient, subject and body already filled in. People only have to press Send. It is an easy way to collect feedback, RSVPs, support requests, sign-ups, quotes and order enquiries from print – without making anyone type an address.",
 ["Enter the e-mail address that should receive messages.","Add a subject, e.g. *Quote request – kitchen*.","Optionally add a body text with prompts like *Name:*, *Phone:*.","Style the code, add a frame like *Email us*, and download."],
 "The code contains a standard *mailto:* link, for example *mailto:hello@example.com?subject=Quote%20request&body=Name%3A*. Spaces and special characters are URL-encoded automatically. Phones open the default mail app – Mail, Gmail, Outlook – and the person can still edit everything before sending.",
 ["Feedback cards in shops, hotels and clinics","Support labels on products and manuals","RSVPs on printed invitations","Lead forms at trade-show stands","Lost-and-found tags on luggage and equipment"],
 ["Use a shared inbox (e.g. hello@ or support@) on public material.","Put a reference in the subject so you can filter messages.","Keep the body short – prompts, not paragraphs.","Print the address as text too."],
 "Email us","the mail app opens with the address, subject and body filled in","email",
 [Q("How do I make a QR code that opens an email?","Enter the address, subject and body, then download the code."),Q("Does it send the email automatically?","No, the person reviews and presses Send."),Q("Can I pre-fill the subject and message?","Yes, both."),Q("Which mail app opens?","The phone's default mail app."),Q("Is it free?","Yes."),Q("Do codes expire?","No."),Q("Is my address uploaded?","No."),Q("Does it work on iPhone and Android?","Yes.")],
 [("SMS QR code","sms-qr-code-generator"),("vCard QR code","vcard-qr-code-generator")],
 [["Ideas for subject and body templates",{"table":[["Use","Subject","Body"],["Product support","Support – Model X200","Serial number: / Problem:"],["Restaurant feedback","Feedback – Table 12","What did you enjoy? / What could be better?"],["Event RSVP","RSVP – Priya & Arjun's wedding","Names attending: / Dietary needs:"],["Quote request","Quote request – Kitchen","Address: / Preferred date:"],["Lost item","Found item – Tag 0142","Where I found it:"]]},"Using a unique subject per code lets you set up mail filters and see which flyer, table or product produced each message – a simple form of tracking without any analytics."],
  ["Email QR code vs a web form","A web form (Google Forms, Typeform) collects structured answers and needs a link, so use [URL to QR code](/url-to-qr-code/) for it. An email code is quicker to set up, feels personal and lets people attach photos – handy for damage reports, warranty claims and proof of purchase. Many businesses use both: email for support, forms for surveys."],
  ["Spam and privacy considerations","An address printed in a code is no more exposed than one printed as text, but public posters do attract automated scans and spam. Use a dedicated address with good spam filtering for public material, and keep personal addresses for private cards. As the code is generated in your browser, the address is not collected by a QR service while you make it."]])
SIMPLE("qr_sms","SMS QR Code Generator – Scan to Send a Text",
 "Free SMS QR code generator: scan to open a text with number and message pre-filled. For opt-ins, voting and support. Logo, frame, SVG. No sign-up.",
 "An SMS QR code opens the phone's messaging app with your number and a ready-written message, so people just press Send. It is ideal for text-to-join lists, competitions and voting, appointment confirmations, parking and service requests, and quick support – anywhere a text is easier than a call or a form.",
 ["Enter the phone number (international format with +).","Write the message, e.g. *JOIN* or *Table 7 needs help*.","Style the code and add a frame like *Text us*.","Download and test on both iPhone and Android."],
 "The code contains an *SMSTO:* or *sms:* string with the number and message, such as *SMSTO:+919876543210:JOIN*. Both iOS and Android camera apps recognise it and open Messages with everything filled in. Standard SMS rates from the sender's plan apply; nothing is sent without the person pressing Send.",
 ["Text-to-join marketing and opt-ins","Competitions, polls and voting","Restaurant and hotel service requests","Parking, taxi and pickup requests","Appointment confirmations and reminders"],
 ["Use keywords that are easy to process, like JOIN or YES.","Follow local opt-in rules for marketing messages.","Use a number that can receive texts.","Print the number and keyword as text too."],
 "Text us","Messages opens with the number and text filled in","SMS",
 [Q("How do I make a QR code that sends a text?","Enter the number and message, then download."),Q("Does it send automatically?","No, the person presses Send."),Q("Does it work on iPhone?","Yes, with the Camera app."),Q("Can I use it for WhatsApp?","Use a wa.me link with the URL QR tool."),Q("Is it free?","Yes."),Q("Does the sender pay?","Normal SMS rates may apply."),Q("Do codes expire?","No."),Q("Is my number uploaded?","No.")],
 [("Phone number QR code","phone-number-qr-code-generator"),("Email QR code","email-qr-code-generator")],
 [["SMS vs WhatsApp QR codes","SMS works on every phone without an app and suits short keywords and service requests. WhatsApp is popular in many countries and supports photos and long chats; create a WhatsApp code with [URL to QR code](/url-to-qr-code/) using *https://wa.me/919876543210?text=Hello* (number in international format without + or spaces). Choose the channel your audience already uses."],
  ["Marketing rules","In many countries marketing texts require clear consent and an easy way to opt out (for example TCPA rules in the US, PECR and GDPR in the UK and EU, and TRAI regulations in India). An SMS code is a good way to collect that consent – the person chooses to text you – but keep a record and honour STOP requests."]])
SIMPLE("qr_event","Event QR Code Generator – Add to Calendar QR",
 "Free event QR code generator: scan to add title, date, time, location and notes to the phone calendar. Logo, frame, SVG. No sign-up, no expiry.",
 "An event QR code adds an appointment straight to the phone's calendar when scanned – title, start and end time, location and description included. Guests do not forget the date, and nobody types the wrong time. Use it on invitations, posters, tickets, school letters, webinar flyers and appointment cards.",
 ["Enter the event title and location.","Set the start and end date and time.","Add a short description – dress code, link or room number.","Style the code with a frame like *Save the date* and download."],
 "The code contains an iCalendar event (the VEVENT format from RFC 5545), for example *BEGIN:VEVENT / SUMMARY:Annual Meetup / DTSTART:20261212T180000 / DTEND:20261212T210000 / LOCATION:Hall B / END:VEVENT*. iPhones and most Android phones show *Add to calendar*; some Android cameras need Google Lens or a scanner app.",
 ["Wedding and party invitations (save the date)","Conference and meetup posters","School and club letters","Webinar and workshop flyers","Appointment cards for clinics and salons"],
 ["Double-check the date and time before printing.","Put the venue address in the location field so maps can find it.","Include an online-meeting link in the description for hybrid events.","Print the date and time as text too."],
 "Save the date","the calendar app offers to add the event at the correct time","event",
 [Q("How do I create a QR code for an event?","Enter the title, times and location, then download."),Q("Can it add to Google Calendar?","Yes, on Android it can be saved to the phone calendar, which syncs with Google Calendar."),Q("Does it work on iPhone?","Yes, it shows Add to calendar."),Q("Can I add a Zoom or Meet link?","Yes, in the description."),Q("Is it free?","Yes."),Q("What about time zones?","Times are used as entered; state the time zone for online events."),Q("Do codes expire?","No, but the event date passes."),Q("Is my data uploaded?","No.")],
 [("Location QR code","location-qr-code-generator"),("URL to QR code","url-to-qr-code")],
 [["Time zones and online events","For in-person events, times are taken as local time where the guest scans, which is what you want. For online events with guests across countries, write the time zone in the title or description (*18:00 IST / 13:30 BST*) and consider sending a calendar invitation link as well. Check daylight-saving changes if the event is months away."],
  ["Event QR code vs a calendar link","Google Calendar and Outlook can create a shareable *add to calendar* link, which you could turn into a code with [URL to QR code](/url-to-qr-code/). That needs internet and an account on the guest's side. An event QR code holds the event itself, works offline and adds to whichever calendar app the guest uses – iCloud, Google, Outlook or Samsung."],
  ["Design ideas for invitations","Match the code colour to the invitation – a deep green, navy or burgundy on cream card looks elegant and still scans well. Use rounded or dot modules for a softer look, a small monogram as the centre logo, and a *Save the date* frame. Print at least 2.5 cm wide on textured paper, and test a printed proof because heavy textures can affect scanning."],
  ["Reminders and updates","The calendar entry belongs to the guest, so you cannot change it later. If the time or venue changes, tell guests directly and, for printed material, issue an updated code. For recurring events, add the next date only – recurring rules are not supported by all phone scanners."]])
SIMPLE("qr_bitcoin","Bitcoin QR Code Generator – Address & Amount",
 "Free Bitcoin QR code generator: wallet address with optional amount and label (BIP21). Logo, colours, SVG. Runs in your browser; nothing uploaded.",
 "A Bitcoin QR code lets someone pay you by scanning with their wallet app – your address, and optionally the amount and a label, are filled in automatically. Copying long addresses by hand is slow and error-prone; a QR code removes that risk. Use it for donations, invoices, shop counters, conference tables and online pages.",
 ["Paste your Bitcoin receiving address from your wallet.","Optionally add an amount in BTC and a label such as *Invoice 1042*.","Style the code and add a frame like *Pay with Bitcoin*.","Download, then scan with your own wallet to confirm the address before sharing."],
 "The code contains a payment URI following BIP21, the Bitcoin standard for payment links: *bitcoin:bc1q…?amount=0.0015&label=Invoice%201042*. Wallets such as Bitcoin Core-compatible apps, BlueWallet, Electrum, Muun, Trust Wallet and exchange apps read it and pre-fill the send screen. The payer always confirms before anything is sent.",
 ["Donation pages and charity posters","Invoices and freelance payment requests","Shop and café counters","Conference and meetup tables","Tip jars for streamers and creators"],
 ["Always scan the final code with your own wallet and compare the address.","Use a fresh receiving address per invoice for privacy.","Amounts are in BTC, not satoshis or fiat.","Never put a private key or seed phrase in a QR code."],
 "Pay with Bitcoin","your wallet shows your exact address and amount","Bitcoin",
 [Q("How do I create a Bitcoin QR code?","Paste your address, optionally add amount and label, and download."),Q("What format is used?","BIP21 bitcoin: payment URIs."),Q("Can I set an amount?","Yes, in BTC."),Q("Which wallets can scan it?","Almost all Bitcoin wallets support BIP21."),Q("Is it safe?","The code only contains your public address; never encode private keys."),Q("Is it free?","Yes."),Q("Is my address uploaded?","No, it is created in your browser."),Q("Do codes expire?","No, but use new addresses for privacy.")],
 [("URL to QR code","url-to-qr-code"),("Invoice generator","invoice-generator")],
 [["Address types","Bitcoin addresses come in several formats: legacy addresses starting with *1*, script addresses starting with *3*, native SegWit (bech32) addresses starting with *bc1q* and Taproot addresses starting with *bc1p*. All can be used in a BIP21 code. Native SegWit and Taproot addresses usually mean lower fees for the sender; modern wallets support all four."],
  ["Security checklist",{"list":["Generate the receiving address in your own wallet – never copy it from an e-mail or chat.","Compare the first and last 6 characters after scanning the finished code.","On printed material in public places, check regularly that nobody has stuck a different code over yours.","Keep seed phrases and private keys offline and never in any QR generator.","Because this page works offline, you can disconnect from the internet before creating the code."]}],
  ["Lightning and other coins","This generator creates on-chain Bitcoin payment codes. For Lightning invoices (starting with *lnbc*) or other cryptocurrencies, copy the payment request or URI from your wallet and use [Text to QR code](/text-to-qr-code/), which encodes it exactly as given."]])
SIMPLE("qr_social","Social Media QR Code – Instagram, TikTok, X",
 "Free social media QR code for Instagram, TikTok, X, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, WhatsApp, Telegram, Threads and more. Logo, frame, SVG. No sign-up.",
 "A social media QR code sends people straight to your profile so they can follow, subscribe or message you in one scan. Pick the platform, type your username, and the correct profile link is built for you – Instagram, TikTok, X (Twitter), Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, WhatsApp, Telegram, GitHub, Threads, Pinterest, Snapchat, Twitch or Reddit.",
 ["Choose the platform.","Type your username or handle (the @ is optional).","Style the code in your brand colours, add the platform or brand logo and a frame like *Follow us*.","Download and scan to check that your profile opens."],
 "The code contains your profile URL, for example *https://instagram.com/yourname* or *https://www.tiktok.com/@yourname*. Phones open it in the platform's app if installed, otherwise in the browser. For WhatsApp, enter your number in international format without + (wa.me/919876543210).",
 ["Shop windows, counters and packaging","Business cards and flyers","Event screens and stage banners","Restaurant menus and receipts","Creator merch, stickers and posters"],
 ["Use one code per platform – or a link-in-bio page for many.","Put the platform name or icon in the frame text.","Keep the handle printed under the code.","Use a profile picture and bio that make following easy."],
 "Follow us","your profile opens in the app","social media",
 [Q("How do I make a QR code for my Instagram?","Choose Instagram, type your username and download."),Q("Which platforms are supported?","Instagram, TikTok, X, Facebook, LinkedIn, YouTube, WhatsApp, Telegram, GitHub, Threads, Pinterest, Snapchat, Twitch and Reddit."),Q("Is it free?","Yes, with no sign-up."),Q("Does it open the app?","Yes, if installed; otherwise the browser."),Q("Can I link several profiles in one code?","Use a link-in-bio page with the URL QR tool."),Q("Can I add a logo?","Yes."),Q("Do codes expire?","No."),Q("What if I change my username?","Create a new code.")],
 [("URL to QR code","url-to-qr-code"),("vCard QR code","vcard-qr-code-generator")],
 [["Platform's own QR codes vs this generator","Instagram, TikTok, Snapchat and others can show a QR or name-tag code inside the app. Those are handy for quick sharing but come in fixed styles, sometimes use proprietary formats only the app can read, and must be screenshotted. Codes made here are standard QR codes that any camera reads, in your own colours, with your logo and frame, and as print-ready SVG for posters and packaging."],
  ["One code or many?",{"table":[["Situation","Best approach"],["One main platform (e.g. Instagram shop)","Single social QR code"],["Two platforms on a flyer","Two small codes with clear labels"],["Many platforms","A link-in-bio page (your site, Linktree etc.) with a [URL QR code](/url-to-qr-code/)"],["Contact plus socials","[vCard QR code](/vcard-qr-code-generator/) with website field"]]}],
  ["Growing followers with QR codes",{"list":["Give a reason to scan: *Follow for daily specials* or *Behind the scenes on TikTok*.","Place codes where people wait – queues, tables, waiting rooms.","Offer a small reward for following, such as a discount on the next visit.","Use the same style on all print materials so people recognise your codes.","Check your analytics in the platform – profile visits from new sources show the code is working."]}],
  ["Worked example: a bakery","A bakery puts an Instagram code on its boxes and paper bags with the frame *Follow @ourbakery for today's bakes*. The code uses the bakery's brown brand colour and a small croissant logo in the centre, with error correction at H. Customers scan at home while unpacking, and the bakery's daily posts about fresh batches bring repeat visits. A TikTok code goes on the counter screen with a *Watch us bake* call to action."],
  ["Usernames, links and changes","Type the username exactly as it appears in the profile – usernames are generally not case-sensitive, but dots and underscores matter. For LinkedIn, use the custom part of your public profile URL (linkedin.com/in/**your-name**). For YouTube, use your @handle. If you rename an account, the old link may stop working, so create a new code and replace printed materials when you can. Codes that link to a page you control are the most future-proof option for long print runs."]])
